# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/ship-4 window (the combined ship candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/ship-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# L1 (TIMED, the CANDIDATE of the first decode ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4, the whole candidate as a traffic profile
# (unaudited): ONE-LINE SUMMARY OF WHAT IS IN THE CANDIDATE: the approved fusion ship profile (W2, engine reuse, the op-fusion set, Lever N, prefix reuse) +
# QWEN_FAST_SDPA_PF_ONEQ=1 + QWEN_FAST_GRID13=1 + octo-T8 (QWEN_FAST_OCTO=live, the octo draft, the attention bundle, the glue levers) + QWEN_FAST_TAP_WINDOW_ALIGNED=1 +
# the host KV tier (32 GiB, verify=sample) with the preconverted checkpoints + the third block's memory plan (KV pool 16,500 blocks, trace region 640 MiB). The same tests
# as C1. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. The candidate is a TRAFFIC profile under
# an owner traffic waiver whose decision is PENDING: it boots in a gate or a smoke and logs the word (c2_serving_job.read_bake refuses a PENDING profile only at the BUILD).
# The two _long tests are the DEEP tests: eight real-code prompts of about 32k / 120k tokens with budgets (3,000 / 4,000, ignore_eos) that outlast the prefill queue, so
# that the last user arrives while the first is still decoding and eight seats decode together at depth; the 800-token concurrent8_code_32k / _128k (run beside them for
# continuity) never have six seats live at once, so no octo round runs in them. READ: c2_smoke_check clean AND python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container
# log> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4 clean: one "[OCTO] admitted mode=live" line, the UNQUALIFIED lines, at least 16 rounds with
# shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 (the positive control: written after the octo block's own verify counter moved), no counted m3 round under live, no program compiled on
# the first octo round, the K64j geometry line (extent replay engaged segments=8 flags=0x21 ... G8B1) and the factory line for the bundle's launch size (entries=4
# kv_share=false), and the lever rules: the octo draft engaged once and serving at least half of the 8-live octo rounds, the bundle engaged ONCE (the latch: the warm and
# the captured fixture build one bundle) with its call line, the glue8 engaged line for every site at users=8 rows=8 and 48 layers, no fallback, disabled or fell-back line
# anywhere. Then the pair: python3 scripts/ci/octo3_report.py --control-a <C1 smoke> --arm-a <L1 smoke> --control-b <C2 smoke> --arm-b <L2 smoke> --arm-container <L1
# container> --arm-container <L2 container> --profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4: per test (concurrent8_steady, concurrent8_code_32k_long,
# concurrent8_code_128k_long) the aggregate of the all-live window against the control's in BOTH pairs, the floors, GAIN / PARITY / LOSS; SHIP-GO needs no LOSS and a GAIN
# in the steady window; octo_compare.py for the texts (EVERY answer equal; any difference is NO-GO). The prefill levers act on prefill, so the 4k, 32k and 120k first tokens
# (prefill_ladder_solo is A1's) are read from the same logs' ttft lines. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every
# chip once a second through the smoke step; read telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A gain
# that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 65 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_code_32k_long,concurrent8_code_128k_long
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=100
